<title>BELGIUM: Belgian cen.bank sees 1997 deficit at 2.8% of GDP.</title>
<headline>Belgian cen.bank sees 1997 deficit at 2.8% of GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said in a statement on Friday it estimated the Belgian state deficit would fall to 2.8 percent of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) in 1997 from a revised 3.2 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>The forecast is below the government's self-set target of 2.9 percent and in line with forecast made by the OECD and private institutions.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6813, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
